<title>BELARUS: SOCCER-SCOTLAND BEAT BELARUS 1-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-SCOTLAND BEAT BELARUS 1-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>MINSK 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scotland beat Belarus 1-0 (halftime</p>
<p>0-0) in their World Cup European zone group four qualifier on</p>
<p>Sunday:</p>
<p>Scorer: Gary McAllister 50 penalty</p>
<p>Belarus - 1-Andrei Satsunkevich; 2-Erik Yakhimovich,</p>
<p>5-Sergei Shtanyuk, 4-Andrei Ostrovsky 3-Andrei Lavrik; 8-Sergei</p>
<p>Gurenko, 7-Sergei Gerasimets, 6-Radislav Orlovsky (15-Dmitry</p>
<p>Balashov, 67), 9-Andrei Dovnar (14-Valentin Belkevich, 54);</p>
<p>10-Miroslav Romashenko, 11-Andrei Khlebosolov (13-Vladimir</p>
<p>Makovsky, 61).</p>
<p>Scotland - 1-Jim Leighton; 3-Tom Boyd, 2-Craig Burley,</p>
<p>6-Tosh McKinlay (15-Brian McAllister, 79); 5-Paul Lambert,</p>
<p>4-Christian Dailly, 7-Kevin Gallacher, 8-David Hopkin (16-Scott</p>
<p>Gemmill, 68); 10-Gary McAllister, 9-Darren Jackson (17-Billy</p>
<p>Dodds, 88), 11-Gordon Durie.</p>
<p>Attendance: 12,000</p>
<p>    Standings	 P   W   D   L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> Scotland	     8   5   2   1   9   2   17</p>
<p> Austria		5   3   1   1   5   3   10</p>
<p> Sweden		 5   3   0   2   9   5    9</p>
<p> Latvia		 6   2   1   3   8   8    7</p>
<p> Estonia		6   1   1   4   2   8    4</p>
<p> Belarus		6   1   1   4   3  10    4</p>
<p>Also playing Sunday: Latvia v Austria, Estonia v Sweden.</p>
</text>
